MODULE 1: TABLE & FLOOR MANAGEMENT
- Live visual floor plan covering 6 tables: T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, and T6.
- Five real-time table statuses with color indicators:
  1. Empty (Grey/Green — ready for guests)
  2. Ordering (Blue — customer browsing QR menu)
  3. Eating (Yellow/Orange — order sent/served)
  4. Bill Requested (Purple — awaiting payment)
  5. Needs Help (Flashing Red — active Call Waiter alert)
- Each table has a unique QR code URL embedding table number and security token (e.g., ?table=T1&token=abc123).
- Active Tables Counter displayed live on Staff and Owner screens (e.g., "6/6 Tables Active").

MODULE 2: CUSTOMER QR MENU & ORDERING (NO LOGIN)
- Scanning the table QR opens the mobile-friendly menu immediately—zero registration, login, or app download required.
- Four menu categories: Main Course, Sides, Drinks, and Deals.
- Dish cards display: Dish Name, Photo, Price (Half & Full), Veg/Non-Veg indicator, Spice Level selector (Mild / Medium / Hot), Allergen tags (Dairy, Nuts, Gluten), and promotional Deal Badges ("Deal of the Day").
- Interactive menu filters: Veg-only toggle, category tabs, allergen exclusion, and live keyword search.
- Interactive shopping cart with item customization, quantity +/- buttons, and live subtotal preview.

MODULE 3: TWO-STEP ORDER FLOW & LIVE TRACKING
- Step 1: Customer places order from phone -> Status becomes "Placed".
- Step 2: Order appears immediately on Staff Tablet -> Staff reviews and clicks "Send to Kitchen" -> Status becomes "Confirmed" -> "Cooking".
- Customer sees live order status progression: Placed -> Confirmed -> Cooking -> Ready -> Served.
- Live Cooking Countdown Timer shown to customer (e.g., "Your food is cooking — 11:30 min left") calculated from estimated_ready_at.
- Full Order History accessible per table session.

MODULE 4: KITCHEN DISPLAY SYSTEM (KDS)
- Screen divided into three specialized kitchen stations: Tandoor, Curry, and Drinks.
- Incoming order items automatically route to their assigned station column.
- Each KDS ticket card displays: Table Number, Dish Name, Portion Size, Spice Level, Quantity, and elapsed cooking timer.
- Color-coded urgency timers:
  - Green: New order (0–5 mins)
  - Yellow: Cooking long (5–12 mins)
  - Red: Late / overdue (>12 mins)
- Kitchen staff actions: "Start Cooking" -> "Mark Ready". Once marked "Served" by floor staff, cards automatically clear from the KDS board.

MODULE 5: GUEST ENGAGEMENT (WHILE WAITING)
- Free WiFi Card: Automatically unlocks and displays the restaurant WiFi Network Name and Password right after placing an order.
- Loyalty Rewards Tracker: Displays guest points balance (e.g., 160 points) with a visual progress bar toward the 200-point milestone ("200 points = Free Mango Lassi").
- Spice Quiz Game: Interactive trivia mini-game about Indian spices and dishes that awards bonus loyalty points.
- Table vs. Table Live Challenge: Real-time points leaderboard comparing active tables (e.g., "T5 vs T2 Live Leaderboard") to encourage group engagement.

MODULE 6: CALL WAITER ALERT SYSTEM
- One-tap "Call Waiter" button on the customer's phone with 4 quick options: Water, Napkins, Bill, or Other Help.
- Triggers an instant popup/sound alert on the Staff Tablet and turns that table Red on the live floor map (e.g., "T5 Needs Help — Water").
- Staff taps "Mark Resolved" upon reaching the table; system calculates exact response time in seconds (e.g., "Waiter Reached in 8 sec") for performance analytics.

MODULE 7: BILLING, SPLIT BILL & PAYMENT
- Automatic consolidated bill generation per table combining all order batches.
- Itemized breakdown showing Dish Name, Size, Quantity, Unit Price, Line Total, Subtotal, 5% GST, Tip, and Grand Total.
- Flexible Bill Splitting options:
  - No Split (Single payment)
  - Equal Split by 2, 3, or 4 people
  - Split by Individual Item
- Tip selector: 5%, 10%, 15%, or Custom Rupee amount.
- Five supported payment methods: Cash, Card, Bank Transfer, Google Pay, and Apple Pay.
- Post-payment workflow: Sends/displays digital receipt, marks bill "Paid", closes all table orders, and resets table status to "Empty".

MODULE 8: POST-PAYMENT FEEDBACK & REVIEW
- Immediately after payment confirmation, customer sees a feedback prompt: "How was your experience?"
- Includes a 1.0 to 5.0 Star Rating selector and an optional comment box.
- Submitted ratings save directly to the database and update the Owner Dashboard's live satisfaction score.

MODULE 9: OWNER DASHBOARD & ADMIN CONTROLS
- Live KPI Cards: Active Tables (e.g., 6/6), Total Orders Today (e.g., 46), Total Revenue Today (e.g., ₹48.6k), Average Rating (e.g., 4.9/5.0).
- Visual Analytics (Plotly): Hourly/Daily Live Sales Chart and Top-Selling Dishes bar chart.
- Staff Performance Tracker: Average waiter response time (in seconds) per staff member for Call Waiter alerts.
- Menu Management: Add new dishes, edit prices/details, toggle dish availability On/Off, or delete items.
- User & Role Management: Create, activate, or deactivate accounts for Staff, Kitchen, and Owner roles.

MODULE 10: ROLES & ACCESS CONTROL
- Customer: No login required (authenticated solely via table QR token). Accesses QR Menu, Cart, Order Tracker, Guest Games/Rewards, Call Waiter, Billing, and Feedback.
- Staff / Waiter: Login required. Accesses Live Floor Map, Order Confirmation ("Send to Kitchen"), Call Waiter Alerts, and Table Billing.
- Kitchen Staff: Login required. Accesses only the 3-Station Kitchen Display System (KDS).
Use code with caution.
• Owner / Admin: Login required. Full access to Owner Analytics Dashboard, Menu Management, Staff Management, Reports, and Audit Logs.

